WEBVTT

00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:04.167
- Previously on The O.C.:
- Can we just start over?

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.375
- Wait.
- Don't you want to?

00:00:06.583 --> 00:00:08.042
No.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.000
- Ryan.
- Theresa.

00:00:10.208 --> 00:00:12.333
- You ever think about coming home?
- Sometimes.

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.208
I know I shouldn't be here.

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:15.833
Would you like to come in?

00:00:16.042 --> 00:00:18.792
It's always been you, Summer.
You're undeniable.

00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:23.500
I'm a man now. I had sex with a girl.
Summer, to be more specific.

00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:25.458
Hi, Marissa. Theresa.

00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:29.250
Okay. Bye.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.000
So you and Marissa, you guys broken up?
You guys taking a break? What's the deal?

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:47.250
I don't know.
We're just not seeing each other.

00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:51.500
Except you will see each other, at school
every day for the next couple years.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:55.542
Right. Well, we'll just
go back to being friends.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.875
When were you guys ever friends?

00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:02.375
Was it when you were beating up her
boyfriend? Or spooning in a Tijuana motel?

00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:05.583
- Is that when you were friends?
- Doesn't mean we can't be friends.

00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:07.167
I don't know.

00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:08.875
Think I'll see her today?

00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.250
Friends, Coop?

00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:14.292
What are you guys gonna do together?
Lift weights? Try on wife-beaters?

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.083
Sorry. Guys like Ryan
aren't friends with girls.

00:01:17.292 --> 00:01:20.458
I don't wanna just be his friend.
But after the whole Oliver thing...

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:23.708
...I guess I need to show him
he can trust me.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.583
Who knows if he'll
even wanna be friends.

00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:30.042
- So how goes it with Seth?
- Weird.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.000
In public, he's like this huge geek
who mumbles.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.625
I don't even know what he's saying half
the time. But behind closed doors...

00:01:36.833 --> 00:01:39.833
...underneath the sheets,
he's like the anti-Cohen.

00:01:40.042 --> 00:01:41.792
You think I'll have to see him today?

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.750
I think me and Summer are finally
over the hump, by the way.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:47.250
So to speak. I just hope, man...

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:50.292
...that she can keep it in her trousers
when she sees me today.

00:01:50.458 --> 00:01:53.208
She'll probably have her little paws
all over me.

00:01:53.833 --> 00:01:56.583
That's probably her now,
a little phone sex.

00:01:57.125 --> 00:01:59.208
Who do I know from the 909?

00:01:59.417 --> 00:02:01.208
Nobody.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.042
- Hello?
- Ryan?

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.083
Hi, it's Theresa.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:10.167
- Yeah, Seth's mom gave me this number.
- Hey. How are you? Everything okay?

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:12.208
Yeah, fine.

00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:15.583
- I'm actually coming out there today.
- You are? How come?

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:18.833
- I mean, for work?
- Yeah...

00:02:19.042 --> 00:02:21.333
...but they can't make us
work all the time, right?

00:02:21.542 --> 00:02:25.333
- I was thinking we could hang out tonight.
- Tonight? Sure.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:30.042
- Don't sound so excited.
- I am. I'm just a little surprised, that's all.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.500
Oh, you know me, full of surprises.
So I'll come by after dinner.

00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:35.708
Yeah, sounds good. See you then.

00:02:36.375 --> 00:02:37.750
Hey, baby. Who's that?

00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:39.792
Wrong number.

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:45.708
That was Theresa.
She's in town, wants to hang out.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.875
As a friend.

00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:50.708
Well, first Marissa, then Theresa.

00:02:50.917 --> 00:02:52.958
Who knew Ryan Atwood was so friendly?

00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:36.500
- Summer.
- Cohen.

00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:38.542
- Ryan.
- Hi.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.333
- Summer. Can we talk?
- Hey, Brad, what's up?

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.708
Brad.

00:03:43.917 --> 00:03:46.667
Dude, I didn't recognize you
out of the Speedo.

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:49.708
Not that I'd recognize you
in a Speedo, but...

00:03:49.917 --> 00:03:52.292
Okay. Come on.

00:03:52.792 --> 00:03:54.542
Jeez.

00:03:58.083 --> 00:04:01.083
- So how are you?
- I'm...

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:05.583
I'm late. See you.

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:11.667
So we're doing a fundraiser for the team,
a kissing booth.

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:14.375
I'm gonna be the guy,
and we're looking for a girl...

00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:17.500
...who's comfortable being paid
to make out with a bunch of guys.

00:04:17.708 --> 00:04:20.958
- Naturally, I thought of you.
- Really? You thought of me?

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.250
God. Totally. I mean, why not?

00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:26.000
- Thanks, Summer.
- Sure.

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:29.458
He talked to you like I wasn't there.
Does he know we're going out?

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:31.417
It's not like he wants to kiss me.

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:34.542
He just wants me to kiss
a bunch of other dudes for money.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.792
I'll see you tonight. My place?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.458
You can help me practice.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.292
- Anna.
- So you guys are together now?

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.500
Well, that didn't take long, did it?

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.125
Yeah, Summer and I are...

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:50.708
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

00:04:50.917 --> 00:04:53.833
I mean, I did see it coming.
It's the reason I broke up with you.

00:04:55.875 --> 00:04:58.458
- Hey, how was Pittsburgh?
- It was good to be home.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:02.500
Pittsburgh's also the home
of Andy Warhol, Mr. Rogers and ketchup.

00:05:02.708 --> 00:05:04.500
- You can't compete with that.
- You can't.

00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:07.917
Yeah, it was really great.
I got a tuna melt at my favorite diner...

00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:10.792
...and I saw Some Kind of Wonderful
at the midnight movie...

00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:13.875
...and hung out with all my friends.
It was really nice.

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.542
Guess I didn't realize
how much I missed them.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.292
Hey, Dad.
You wanted to see me?

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:22.833
Kiki, we got a problem.

00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:26.417
- Uncle Shaun was arrested last night.
- You're kidding. For what?

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:29.375
He was drunk, stumbled into
another guest's room at the St. Regis.

00:05:29.917 --> 00:05:32.292
He's been stumbling around drunk
since you met him...

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.542
...which was in a bar.
I'll have someone in Legal handle it.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.875
- I was thinking you might ask Sandy.
- Very funny.

00:05:39.083 --> 00:05:41.958
He knows people at the DA's office.
He can make this go away.

00:05:42.167 --> 00:05:43.958
- He'll never do it.
- Why not?

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:47.000
- Because it would be a favor to me?
- Pretty much. Yeah.

00:05:47.208 --> 00:05:49.458
You could tell him
it would mean a lot to you.

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:52.458
Actually, it would mean a lot to me.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.208
But if you want Sandy's help
after all these years...

00:05:55.417 --> 00:05:59.667
...then you need to ask him,
because that would mean a lot to Sandy.

00:06:02.958 --> 00:06:05.292
- No.
- You should see these two guys.

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.500
- Oh, come on.
- Honestly, it was unbelievable.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.042
I swear to God.

00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:12.292
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:06:13.042 --> 00:06:16.125
So this is you and Summer
being a couple?

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.167
- Ain't love grand?
- I can really sense the bond.

00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:23.625
It's like, your closeness,
it's overwhelming.

00:06:23.833 --> 00:06:25.417
Oh, my gosh. Wait.

00:06:25.625 --> 00:06:27.750
Is it last fall already?

00:06:27.958 --> 00:06:31.375
- Come on, she's totally ignoring you.
- Anna, she's not ignoring me.

00:06:31.583 --> 00:06:35.458
Summer just has her priorities in order.
You know how she feels about charity.

00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:41.667
- Yes?
- Yeah. Good luck with that.

00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:57.625
Mrs. Cooper.

00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:00.667
- What are you doing here?
- Parent-teacher conference.

00:07:00.833 --> 00:07:04.458
- It's good to see you.
- It's good to see you too.

00:07:05.167 --> 00:07:08.292
Really good. You... I mean...
God, you look good.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:12.208
Luke, I'm Marissa's mother.
You're a student at this school.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:16.333
- We can't do this.
- You mean it's over?

00:07:16.542 --> 00:07:18.375
No, I mean in the hallway.

00:07:18.583 --> 00:07:20.375
I'll see you tonight.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.542
- Hey, Julie.
- Jimmy, hi.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.000
- You remember Luke.
- Who could forget?

00:07:25.208 --> 00:07:26.750
- Luke.
- Hey, Mr. Cooper.

00:07:26.917 --> 00:07:30.792
I'm glad you're here. I didn't want to go
to Dr. Kim's office alone. She scares me.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.292
Okay, well, goodbye, Mrs. Cooper.
And Mr. Cooper.

00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:36.875
I'll see you.

00:07:37.083 --> 00:07:38.667
Both.

00:07:42.125 --> 00:07:44.167
Have a good day.

00:07:49.708 --> 00:07:52.542
Hey, I'm sorry about this morning.
That...

00:07:52.708 --> 00:07:54.958
- It shouldn't have to be...
- Like this?

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:58.917
I was just sort of hoping
we could be friends, you know?

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:02.458
- I mean, as long as that's okay with you.
- Yeah. No, we should hang out.

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:05.542
Okay.
What are you doing tonight?

00:08:06.042 --> 00:08:09.167
- Tonight's no good.
- It's okay. We don't have to do this.

00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:11.292
What about after school?

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.625
Actually, after school's good.
It's better...

00:08:13.833 --> 00:08:16.708
...because I'm supposed to have dinner
with my dad. Your place?

00:08:16.917 --> 00:08:18.917
- Yeah, see you then.
- Cool.

00:08:27.333 --> 00:08:28.792
Well...

00:08:28.958 --> 00:08:32.667
...the restaurant's coming along, Sandy.
At this rate, you'll be open by 2008.

00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:34.958
And there goes my appetite.
Caleb, hello.

00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:38.500
- What the hell is that?
- It's my mother's meat loaf.

00:08:38.708 --> 00:08:40.542
- God, your mother's here?
- Her recipe is.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:44.458
- We're trying out a chef. You want some?
- The sight of your mother's meat loaf...

00:08:44.667 --> 00:08:47.125
...has turned me into a vegetarian.

00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:51.250
I know you're a big fan of the pop-in, but
is there another reason why you're here?

00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:53.625
I've come to ask a favor.

00:08:53.917 --> 00:08:55.292
I'm sorry, what did you say?

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.792
- You didn't hear me?
- I heard you. I want you to say it again.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.208
- A friend is in trouble. I want you to help.
- I didn't know you had friends.

00:09:02.417 --> 00:09:04.917
- It's Bill Shaughnessy.
- Uncle Shaun.

00:09:05.125 --> 00:09:09.167
You pay Uncle Shaun to be your friend.
I guess he qualifies. What did he do?

00:09:09.333 --> 00:09:12.292
He was drinking, stumbled into
someone else's hotel room.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.875
They called security,
and now it's a legal matter.

00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:19.792
- You've got lawyers at your beck and call.
- He came to me as a friend.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.542
I want it handled like a friend.
Quietly.

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:25.292
By someone who has a relationship
with the DA's office?

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:29.542
I'm asking you.
I've known Shaun for over 40 years.

00:09:29.708 --> 00:09:31.458
It would mean a lot to me.

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:36.000
- Did Kirsten tell you to say that?
- She thinks you'll say no.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.458
My wife knows me pretty well.

00:09:38.667 --> 00:09:40.792
But, you know,
sometimes I like to surprise her.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.625
I don't want her to go and get all
conceited and stuff, you know?

00:09:44.833 --> 00:09:48.208
You have a copy of the police report?
Now, I'm not saying that I'll do it.

00:09:48.417 --> 00:09:52.917
I'm saying that I'll look at the report,
I'll make some calls and then we'll see.

00:09:56.292 --> 00:09:58.833
- Got any more of that meat loaf?
- Maybe.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:02.958
Well, that was a relief. Dr. Kim seems
to think Marissa's doing well.

00:10:03.167 --> 00:10:05.542
I was sure she was gonna revoke
my license to parent.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:08.292
You know, Jimmy,
I don't think I ever thanked you.

00:10:08.958 --> 00:10:12.250
That's not true. You've thanked me
for alienating the community...

00:10:12.458 --> 00:10:15.458
...destroying the family.
- For doing a wonderful job with Marissa.

00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:18.292
I'm serious.
Listening to you in that meeting...

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:22.792
...you're totally involved in her life.
- You and Caleb must be doing really well.

00:10:23.458 --> 00:10:27.083
- Why would you say that?
- Because you're being so...

00:10:27.292 --> 00:10:29.375
...nice.
- Well, actually...

00:10:29.583 --> 00:10:32.750
...Caleb and I aren't
seeing each other anymore.

00:10:32.958 --> 00:10:34.500
And I'm much happier.

00:10:36.208 --> 00:10:40.667
And to think, you've spent a lifetime
wanting to be rich and married...

00:10:40.833 --> 00:10:43.958
...when what agrees with you most
is being poor and alone.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.542
Isn't it better when we're alone?
Just the two of us?

00:10:53.208 --> 00:10:55.958
- Why did you ignore me at school today?
- I didn't ignore you.

00:10:57.667 --> 00:11:00.125
Okay, maybe a little.

00:11:00.333 --> 00:11:03.292
I just... I want our relationship
to be private, okay?

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.750
I don't like other people
knowing my business.

00:11:05.958 --> 00:11:08.625
- Why not?
- Because it's none of their business.

00:11:08.875 --> 00:11:12.042
Look, there's, like, pressure...

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.667
...and scrutiny in the spotlight.
- What spotlight?

00:11:15.875 --> 00:11:18.792
When has being in the public eye
ever helped a relationship?

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:22.417
Sure, we're this week's hottest couple,
but then the world gets sick of it.

00:11:22.625 --> 00:11:25.625
The shopping sprees, the strip clubs.
People turn against us, okay?

00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:27.792
"How many Juicy sweat suits
does she need?"

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.958
"That goatee is so mid-'90s." Pretty soon,
the movie bombs and the wedding is off!

00:11:33.375 --> 00:11:36.625
But I'm not gonna let that
happen to us, because, Cohen...

00:11:36.833 --> 00:11:38.292
...what we have is special.

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:40.458
Summer...

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.458
...that's maybe just...

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.333
- Guess I'm not very good.
- Yeah.

00:11:53.542 --> 00:11:56.208
Want a rematch?
Because I couldn't possibly get any worse.

00:11:56.417 --> 00:11:59.583
No, I should probably
start on my homework.

00:11:59.792 --> 00:12:03.542
Oh, yeah, me too.
I mean, my dad's probably waiting.

00:12:04.542 --> 00:12:08.250
- Is this...? I don't know, are we...?
- Why...? Why is this weird?

00:12:08.458 --> 00:12:11.125
- It shouldn't be.
- We used to hang out all the time and...

00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:13.167
Make out?

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.792
- We could always fight about Luke.
- Or Oliver.

00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:22.250
Sorry. I just...

00:12:24.083 --> 00:12:25.292
Hey, Ryan.

00:12:26.333 --> 00:12:27.958
Hey, Marissa.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.917
I'm early. Sorry.
I'll go and come back later.

00:12:33.125 --> 00:12:34.833
It's okay.
We weren't doing anything.

00:12:35.042 --> 00:12:37.875
Yeah, I was just leaving.
He's got a lot of homework.

00:12:38.333 --> 00:12:39.625
Good to see you, Theresa.

00:12:40.083 --> 00:12:41.958
It's nice to see you too.

00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:46.250
The ninja game?

00:12:46.458 --> 00:12:48.625
You're dead now.

00:12:52.875 --> 00:12:54.958
Considering he is your "Uncle" Shaun...

00:12:55.167 --> 00:12:57.458
...don't you think it's weird
we have never met?

00:12:58.167 --> 00:13:01.042
He's not really my uncle.

00:13:01.292 --> 00:13:03.792
- And he pretty much works all the time.
- Doing what?

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.458
He's a consultant.

00:13:05.625 --> 00:13:08.542
Could you please be a little more vague?

00:13:08.708 --> 00:13:10.250
He knows people.

00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:12.875
You did it.
That was more vague.

00:13:13.083 --> 00:13:16.208
The guys at the permit office,
the union guys.

00:13:16.417 --> 00:13:18.542
He's our liaison.

00:13:21.375 --> 00:13:24.542
Well, I looked over the police report,
I put in a few calls...

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.542
...and I'm sure I'll hear something back
before we get together tonight.

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.000
- Thank you.
- Overexposure, Ryan...

00:13:31.208 --> 00:13:34.292
...it's a major source of conflict
in new relationships.

00:13:34.458 --> 00:13:37.583
"Summereth." "Sethummer."
You understand what I'm saying?

00:13:37.792 --> 00:13:40.708
- No. No. That's normal.
- Ryan, your friend Theresa called.

00:13:41.083 --> 00:13:44.458
- I'd like to meet Theresa.
- Yeah, she'd like to meet you guys.

00:13:44.667 --> 00:13:47.417
- What's she doing here?
- Taking a semester off, making money.

00:13:47.625 --> 00:13:51.042
Catering a tennis tournament.
Her mom got laid off.

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.917
So she's out here a while.
Does Marissa know? I'm curious.

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.417
They kind of bumped into each other.

00:13:56.625 --> 00:13:59.625
Look at you, the friend guy.
Bringing friends together.

00:13:59.833 --> 00:14:01.750
- I sense sarcasm.
- You're perceptive.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:05.875
This mysterious caliente female from
your past just shows up out of nowhere...

00:14:06.083 --> 00:14:09.958
...with all this time on her hands
and no one to spend it with but you.

00:14:10.167 --> 00:14:13.708
- Marissa okay with this?
- She's fine. They're back to being friends.

00:14:13.917 --> 00:14:15.625
So when were they ever friends?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.875
You are so beautiful, you know that?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.208
You're very sweet.

00:14:30.417 --> 00:14:33.750
- I wish we could stay here forever.
- Why?

00:14:33.958 --> 00:14:37.875
We got everything we need here.
We got our bed. We got our cable.

00:14:38.083 --> 00:14:39.917
We got each other.

00:14:40.458 --> 00:14:43.042
- This place is awesome.
- It's not awesome.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:45.750
It's $ 79 a night.

00:14:46.333 --> 00:14:49.875
I gotta motor.
I don't wanna be late for homeroom.

00:14:50.125 --> 00:14:51.875
You have homeroom.

00:14:52.083 --> 00:14:54.542
Right. Because you're in high school.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.333
And you're only 18.

00:15:01.417 --> 00:15:04.167
Kaitlin, are you okay?

00:15:05.042 --> 00:15:06.500
You're in front of the house?

00:15:06.667 --> 00:15:10.333
Chester's mom was supposed to pick you
up at Grandma's and take you to school.

00:15:11.667 --> 00:15:13.750
Your diorama.

00:15:14.167 --> 00:15:16.750
Yeah, I think it's
in the living room, honey.

00:15:16.958 --> 00:15:20.375
Okay, just wait there with Grandma.
I'll be there as soon as I can.

00:15:20.708 --> 00:15:22.167
Okay. See you soon.

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.875
- See you tonight?
- Oh, Luke.

00:15:27.083 --> 00:15:29.833
Motels, homerooms, dioramas.

00:15:30.042 --> 00:15:34.083
- This is not the stuff of great romance.
- But, Mrs...

00:15:34.417 --> 00:15:36.167
Julie.

00:15:37.375 --> 00:15:39.208
I'm sorry.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.458
- No worries.
- Good.

00:16:11.542 --> 00:16:13.000
Hey.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:15.792
- You mind if...?
- No.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:17.708
Thanks.

00:16:20.458 --> 00:16:22.875
- So, sorry about...
- Sorry I was such a...

00:16:24.375 --> 00:16:27.042
- I should've told you she was coming.
- You didn't have to.

00:16:27.208 --> 00:16:29.875
But you could've.
I mean, now that we're friends, right?

00:16:30.042 --> 00:16:33.625
- Right.
- So you and Theresa...?

00:16:34.167 --> 00:16:37.000
- We're friends.
- And she's back in town for...?

00:16:37.208 --> 00:16:39.875
Work. She's staying
till the end of the week.

00:16:40.875 --> 00:16:44.708
- Where's she staying?
- The motel by the pier.

00:16:44.917 --> 00:16:47.042
The Seashell? Sea Monkey?

00:16:47.542 --> 00:16:50.000
- The Mermaid.
- Right.

00:16:50.208 --> 00:16:53.542
- Next week we could have that rematch.
- Think you're up for it?

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:56.792
Hey, what I lack in nunchaku,
I make up for in saber.

00:16:58.375 --> 00:16:59.833
So...

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:02.417
...did you talk to Summer yesterday?
- Yeah.

00:17:02.625 --> 00:17:06.000
- Oh, yeah?
- We talked about school...

00:17:06.208 --> 00:17:08.083
...and sports and the weather.

00:17:08.292 --> 00:17:11.208
But if you're referring to the part
where she's ashamed of me, no.

00:17:11.375 --> 00:17:12.958
Didn't get to that.

00:17:14.042 --> 00:17:18.083
Were you gonna say something?
Something very wise and helpful, Anna?

00:17:18.542 --> 00:17:21.875
- No.
- You got nothing? No advice at all for me?

00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:24.583
- I feel like you did.
- Why do I do this?

00:17:24.792 --> 00:17:27.125
Because you're so wise, Anna.
You can't not.

00:17:27.333 --> 00:17:30.375
All right, fine.
Look, you have to take a stand, all right?

00:17:30.583 --> 00:17:32.500
You can't let her get away with it.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:34.833
Otherwise she has something
to be ashamed of...

00:17:35.042 --> 00:17:37.458
...because then her boyfriend
is a coward.

00:17:40.875 --> 00:17:44.792
I'm just going to help with the kissing
booth, you know, because I love to help.

00:17:46.417 --> 00:17:48.833
Right, coward. Got it.

00:17:52.667 --> 00:17:55.583
Hope you don't mind.
I let myself in through the back.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.125
It's what you do.
Famous Uncle Shaun.

00:17:58.458 --> 00:18:01.833
Here. Famous Grouse.

00:18:02.042 --> 00:18:04.792
I haven't seen a bottle of this
since Bob Mitchum passed.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.917
- You knew Robert Mitchum?
- Yeah. He and his wife Dorothy...

00:18:08.083 --> 00:18:12.500
...they used to have a place over there
on Linda Isle.

00:18:13.083 --> 00:18:17.208
That was their favorite booth.
Sunday dinners. Chicken parm.

00:18:17.375 --> 00:18:21.208
I'm partial to the parm myself,
and a lover of blended Scotch.

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:25.125
And Caleb keeps saying
you have no redeeming qualities.

00:18:27.583 --> 00:18:30.500
So I read the police report.
I just have a couple of questions.

00:18:30.667 --> 00:18:33.875
This fellow who's pressing charges,
he's in the construction business.

00:18:34.083 --> 00:18:36.833
- Really?
- Yeah. Yeah, he's a lumber supplier...

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:41.458
...one of the biggest in the country.
In fact, he was in town on a negotiation...

00:18:41.625 --> 00:18:43.875
...with one of the Newport Group's
chief rivals.

00:18:44.208 --> 00:18:46.042
- Imagine that.
- Yeah, I'm guessing...

00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:49.542
...that in that room
that you accidentally stumbled into...

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.625
...were documents
containing information...

00:18:51.833 --> 00:18:54.958
...that would be very valuable
to somebody like Caleb.

00:18:55.167 --> 00:18:58.542
- You think?
- You expect me or the DA's office...

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:03.500
...to believe a bellyful of liquor or a wild
coincidence would put you in that room?

00:19:04.583 --> 00:19:06.208
You were there for Caleb.

00:19:06.417 --> 00:19:08.708
That's an interesting theory.

00:19:08.917 --> 00:19:13.625
And one I, you know, hope you don't
explore too much, because...

00:19:13.833 --> 00:19:18.083
What is it, "Sandy"? You know, Caleb
and I have been friends for many years.

00:19:18.292 --> 00:19:21.208
And if I were to sit down with the DA...

00:19:21.417 --> 00:19:24.875
...there's no telling
what we might talk about.

00:19:32.917 --> 00:19:34.542
- So, what do you think?
- It's good.

00:19:36.583 --> 00:19:39.833
- They call them Balboa Bars.
- It's just ice cream.

00:19:40.042 --> 00:19:42.125
No such thing
as just ice cream in Newport.

00:19:42.333 --> 00:19:46.250
Like, instead of car washes,
they have auto spas.

00:19:46.542 --> 00:19:49.292
Dogs have daycare.
Fashion Island has valet parking.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.250
It's a weird place.

00:19:51.458 --> 00:19:53.792
Still, it's beautiful.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.708
I can see why you wanna live here,
start over.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.333
Is that why you came back here?
Start over?

00:20:01.917 --> 00:20:04.583
No, I couldn't.

00:20:04.958 --> 00:20:07.083
I've got my mom to think about.

00:20:07.292 --> 00:20:10.125
My brother. And Eddie.

00:20:12.042 --> 00:20:13.500
You guys are still...?

00:20:13.667 --> 00:20:17.875
We're taking some time apart. You know,
to see if we really belong together.

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:22.083
- What about you and Marissa?
- Kind of the same thing, I guess.

00:20:22.292 --> 00:20:25.625
We're trying to be friends,
but it hasn't exactly been easy.

00:20:25.833 --> 00:20:28.917
- Actually, it's never really been...
- Like this.

00:20:30.792 --> 00:20:34.833
- That's because I never really liked you.
- True. Makes things easier.

00:20:53.917 --> 00:20:56.375
Do you need to stretch
so you won't pull a hammy?

00:20:56.583 --> 00:20:59.750
- Or are you ready for your workout?
- I'm sorry, Summer.

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:03.708
I need to take a stand. This separation
of the public and private spheres...

00:21:03.917 --> 00:21:06.750
...isn't working for me. I can't do it.
- But I told you how...

00:21:06.917 --> 00:21:09.167
One day you might have
some MTV-driven radio hits...

00:21:09.375 --> 00:21:11.375
...and then a moderately priced
clothing line.

00:21:11.583 --> 00:21:16.125
I could get offered $20 million to portray
a blind superhero in a red leather unitard.

00:21:16.333 --> 00:21:20.375
But until then, as long as we're
complete faceless nobodies...

00:21:20.542 --> 00:21:22.250
...living in obscurity...

00:21:23.208 --> 00:21:26.542
...I can't acknowledge you privately
if you won't acknowledge me publicly.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:29.583
Let me know when you're ready
to come to the bargaining table.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:31.625
Until then, just consider me on strike.

00:21:31.833 --> 00:21:33.875
You'll cross your own picket line
in no time.

00:21:34.083 --> 00:21:35.875
Fight the power.

00:21:41.583 --> 00:21:44.250
- Eddie.
- Hey.

00:21:44.417 --> 00:21:47.958
- Hey, man.
- How's it going, Ryan? Good to see you.

00:21:48.958 --> 00:21:50.708
You look good.

00:21:50.917 --> 00:21:52.625
You look good, man.

00:21:52.833 --> 00:21:55.667
Yeah, I went up and visited
your brother last week.

00:21:55.833 --> 00:21:58.708
It kills me he's still serving time.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.542
- Sucks, huh?
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:05.667
It's been a while, man.
What are you doing here?

00:22:05.875 --> 00:22:08.708
Well, actually...

00:22:09.333 --> 00:22:10.708
...I'm looking for Theresa.

00:22:11.083 --> 00:22:12.333
Theresa?

00:22:12.542 --> 00:22:17.083
Yeah, you know, her mom said
she was working out here in Newport...

00:22:17.292 --> 00:22:21.417
...and your brother said you were living
the life out here, you know, so I...

00:22:21.583 --> 00:22:25.167
- I thought maybe you'd seen her.
- She didn't leave a note or something?

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:27.875
No.

00:22:28.042 --> 00:22:29.583
Nothing.

00:22:30.042 --> 00:22:32.875
Some thanks for the ring I got her, huh?

00:22:33.042 --> 00:22:36.167
- Ring?
- Yeah, we're engaged.

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:38.500
Engaged?

00:22:41.833 --> 00:22:44.167
Damn, Eddie, that's great, man.

00:22:44.417 --> 00:22:46.208
Yeah. Yeah, it is.

00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:50.375
So she...

00:22:50.583 --> 00:22:53.083
I mean, she hasn't looked you up at all?

00:22:53.292 --> 00:22:55.542
No, sorry.

00:23:00.417 --> 00:23:04.625
- You're living the dream out here, huh?
- Yeah, you said it.

00:23:04.833 --> 00:23:06.458
That's all right. You deserve it.

00:23:06.958 --> 00:23:09.500
You know, putting up with Trey
for all those years.

00:23:14.542 --> 00:23:18.042
All right.
I'm gonna get out of here.

00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.458
But...

00:23:22.708 --> 00:23:26.542
- Hey, if you see her, you know, just...
- Yeah.

00:23:31.917 --> 00:23:34.042
I don't know, I just...

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:37.125
I can't believe she'd
run out on me like that.

00:23:39.083 --> 00:23:40.292
Neither can I.

00:23:46.042 --> 00:23:48.708
- Were you gonna tell me you're engaged?
- I'm not engaged.

00:23:48.875 --> 00:23:52.333
- What the hell are you doing?
- He asked, I didn't say yes.

00:23:52.542 --> 00:23:55.208
- So you took off. That'll fix everything?
- You did.

00:23:56.833 --> 00:23:58.542
Sorry.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.292
You're gonna have to face him
sooner or later.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:04.625
- I just need time to think.
- Yeah, you need about five years.

00:24:04.833 --> 00:24:07.250
- You're 17.
- What's gonna be different in five years?

00:24:07.458 --> 00:24:09.667
Or have you forgotten
where you come from?

00:24:09.875 --> 00:24:12.625
Not everybody has an infinity pool,
goes to private school...

00:24:12.833 --> 00:24:15.167
...and drives a Range Rover.
- What are you saying?

00:24:15.375 --> 00:24:19.250
Eddie has his own place, he's a foreman at
work and isn't a screwup like his friends.

00:24:19.458 --> 00:24:22.208
- All good reasons to marry him.
- And he loves me.

00:24:24.917 --> 00:24:27.500
- And you?
- I just need time.

00:24:38.417 --> 00:24:40.958
- What are you doing for dinner?
- Nothing.

00:24:41.208 --> 00:24:43.958
- Don't say you're not hungry.
- I didn't say I wasn't hungry.

00:24:44.208 --> 00:24:46.583
I'm starving.
Why do you think I'm being a bitch?

00:24:47.042 --> 00:24:50.042
What are you gonna do, eat out of
the vending machine? Come on.

00:24:50.208 --> 00:24:52.000
Come on.
Come to my house with me.

00:24:53.042 --> 00:24:55.042
You just need a ride.

00:24:56.083 --> 00:24:58.083
Upstairs, alone. Now.

00:24:58.292 --> 00:25:02.167
Upstairs alone? I'm afraid I'd have to
file a grievance with the union.

00:25:02.375 --> 00:25:04.417
- I've had enough.
- I left you two hours ago.

00:25:04.625 --> 00:25:07.708
Well, it feels like four.
I've been thinking about what you said...

00:25:07.875 --> 00:25:11.375
...and I find it totally insensitive.
- I'm being insensitive? Really? How?

00:25:11.583 --> 00:25:14.875
Can't you accept that I'm uncomfortable
with public displays of affection?

00:25:15.208 --> 00:25:17.875
You're offering yourself for $ 10 a pop
at a kissing booth.

00:25:18.042 --> 00:25:21.125
How much more publicly
can affection be displayed?

00:25:21.292 --> 00:25:25.250
I know there's a strike,
but technically...

00:25:25.458 --> 00:25:29.000
...you wouldn't be considered a scab...
- Summer, don't say "scab."

00:25:29.583 --> 00:25:31.500
If you didn't have to do anything.

00:25:35.375 --> 00:25:37.833
Well, your strike-busting techniques
are no good here.

00:25:38.042 --> 00:25:41.125
Sorry, the rank and file
are holding strong.

00:25:42.167 --> 00:25:43.708
Solidarity.

00:25:46.375 --> 00:25:47.583
Cal.

00:25:48.250 --> 00:25:50.333
- What a surprise.
- A welcome one, I hope.

00:25:50.542 --> 00:25:53.625
Well, that depends.

00:25:53.792 --> 00:25:56.167
You've brought flowers?

00:25:59.167 --> 00:26:01.042
Thank you. They're beautiful.

00:26:01.250 --> 00:26:03.500
- I missed you.
- I've missed you too.

00:26:03.708 --> 00:26:07.542
Neither of us are love-struck adolescents
looking to be swept off our feet.

00:26:07.750 --> 00:26:11.875
We're both adults. Our lives
are full of responsibilities, difficulties.

00:26:12.042 --> 00:26:13.917
Well, isn't this romantic.

00:26:14.125 --> 00:26:16.333
We should be able
to come to some arrangement...

00:26:16.542 --> 00:26:19.625
...where we both get from a relationship
what we want.

00:26:20.375 --> 00:26:22.792
Is this a booty call?

00:26:23.167 --> 00:26:24.875
What's a booty call?

00:26:25.042 --> 00:26:28.125
It's when you show up at night,
unannounced, no apologies...

00:26:28.333 --> 00:26:30.917
...no compliments, no commitments...

00:26:31.125 --> 00:26:34.500
...just some crappy mini-carns
from Ralphs...

00:26:34.708 --> 00:26:36.958
...and a very mistaken idea
that I just might wanna...

00:26:46.917 --> 00:26:48.458
Guess it was a booty call.

00:26:48.625 --> 00:26:51.167
How much are you involved
with Uncle Shaun, day-to-day?

00:26:52.417 --> 00:26:53.875
Not much.

00:26:54.042 --> 00:26:56.208
He spends most of his time
out of the office...

00:26:56.417 --> 00:26:58.583
...on site with the crews,
suppliers, inspectors.

00:26:58.792 --> 00:27:02.167
You gotta be a hard-ass to be good
at that job. Lots of tough characters.

00:27:02.875 --> 00:27:05.708
I'm sure Shaun can be persuasive
when he needs to be.

00:27:05.875 --> 00:27:08.708
Convincing-argument persuasive,
or baseball-bat persuasive?

00:27:08.917 --> 00:27:13.375
If you don't wanna help him, I understand.
I didn't think you'd do it in the first place.

00:27:13.583 --> 00:27:18.042
Hey, dinner's ready.
Slaved over hot take-out containers.

00:27:18.250 --> 00:27:20.250
- Ryan here?
- Hey.

00:27:21.667 --> 00:27:23.500
- This is Theresa.
- Hi.

00:27:23.708 --> 00:27:25.750
- Hello, friend.
- Nice to meet you.

00:27:25.958 --> 00:27:27.750
I'm Kirsten. And this is...

00:27:27.958 --> 00:27:30.875
Sandy. Hi.
I've heard so much about you.

00:27:31.042 --> 00:27:33.542
It's nice to meet you all.
Can I help? It looks great.

00:27:33.750 --> 00:27:38.500
Sure. The key is taking the food
out of the Styrofoam containers.

00:27:38.708 --> 00:27:40.583
But her real specialty is ordering.

00:27:40.792 --> 00:27:43.083
Is the silverware in the drawer or...?

00:27:43.292 --> 00:27:46.833
What's going on? Don't say "nothing,"
because it's not nothing. It's something.

00:27:47.042 --> 00:27:49.792
- She's engaged.
- Wow. You make quick work of the ladies.

00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:52.667
- To this guy Eddie.
- Oh, she just told you?

00:27:52.833 --> 00:27:56.000
No, he did, when he showed up
looking for her.

00:27:59.708 --> 00:28:00.917
What's going on here?

00:28:01.125 --> 00:28:04.583
- And don't say "nothing."
- Because it's not nothing. It's something.

00:28:04.792 --> 00:28:07.042
What we have here
is our very own telenovela.

00:28:07.250 --> 00:28:09.917
- Telenovela?
- Yeah. Spanish-language soap opera.

00:28:10.083 --> 00:28:13.708
Ni Ía Amada M Âa.
I hope Isabela gets Victor.

00:28:13.917 --> 00:28:15.375
I love his handlebar moustache.

00:28:15.875 --> 00:28:17.500
- You do it.
- Give it to me.

00:28:21.542 --> 00:28:24.292
Previously on The Valley:

00:28:26.625 --> 00:28:28.333
Hey.

00:28:28.750 --> 00:28:32.167
What are you doing home?
I thought you'd be over at Ryan's house.

00:28:32.375 --> 00:28:35.458
He's kind of busy.
A friend from home.

00:28:35.625 --> 00:28:38.875
- Theresa.
- And you're okay with that?

00:28:39.083 --> 00:28:41.750
- Yeah. It's not a big deal.
- It is kind of a big deal.

00:28:41.917 --> 00:28:44.167
- He's important to you.
- What's important to me...

00:28:44.375 --> 00:28:48.250
...is that we not talk about this right now,
because I'm fine.

00:28:48.792 --> 00:28:51.625
It's just high school.

00:28:52.500 --> 00:28:55.500
Hey, that's supposed to be my line, okay?
You're supposed to say...

00:28:55.708 --> 00:28:59.625
...I could never understand. And how Ryan
is the most important thing in the world...

00:28:59.833 --> 00:29:02.583
...and without him...
- We're just friends.

00:29:02.750 --> 00:29:06.875
- Or at least we're trying to be.
- Look, at the risk of embarrassing you...

00:29:07.042 --> 00:29:08.875
...you and Ryan...

00:29:09.625 --> 00:29:11.750
...never friends.
- So I've been told.

00:29:11.958 --> 00:29:15.458
- But if we can't be friends, then...
- Let him know what you wanna be.

00:29:17.083 --> 00:29:19.833
See? There's still room around here
for me to be the adult.

00:29:20.042 --> 00:29:21.833
Okay?

00:29:24.458 --> 00:29:26.833
So we're all dressed up
for my brother's 16th birthday.

00:29:27.042 --> 00:29:31.167
Not this one. Don't you have anything
that doesn't involve me falling down?

00:29:31.333 --> 00:29:33.833
Did Ryan fall down when he did musicals?
Tell us.

00:29:34.042 --> 00:29:37.875
You did musicals?
I did a musical or two myself in college.

00:29:38.083 --> 00:29:41.167
Someone stop him before he starts
singing "Greased Lightnin'."

00:29:41.375 --> 00:29:43.000
Do it, Dad. Travolta's your bitch.

00:29:43.208 --> 00:29:44.917
- Thank you, son.
- Go ahead.

00:29:45.083 --> 00:29:47.542
We were at the Holiday Inn,
at the revolving restaurant...

00:29:47.750 --> 00:29:50.833
...and Ryan has this thing about heights...
- I'll get it.

00:29:51.042 --> 00:29:52.667
Excuse me.

00:29:55.750 --> 00:29:58.042
- Hey, sweetie.
- Hey.

00:29:58.250 --> 00:30:00.750
- Is Ryan here?
- Yes, he is.

00:30:00.958 --> 00:30:03.333
- I love revolving restaurants.
- Who doesn't?

00:30:03.542 --> 00:30:05.833
Motion and digestion,
unbeatable combination.

00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:08.708
Look who's here.

00:30:09.833 --> 00:30:11.875
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:30:15.208 --> 00:30:17.333
Does everybody know everybody?

00:30:17.542 --> 00:30:20.000
- Yeah. Hi, Theresa.
- Hi, Marissa.

00:30:22.208 --> 00:30:25.833
- You hungry?
- Actually, I'm starved. Is it okay?

00:30:26.042 --> 00:30:27.917
- Sure.
- Absolutely. Have a seat.

00:30:28.125 --> 00:30:30.708
Let me get you a plate.

00:30:39.083 --> 00:30:41.917
So, what's everyone talking about?

00:30:49.833 --> 00:30:52.792
Hey, man, phone for you.
It's Eddie.

00:30:57.250 --> 00:31:00.500
Hey, man, I can't find him.
Do you want me to take a message?

00:31:00.792 --> 00:31:02.708
Apparently not. He hung up.

00:31:02.917 --> 00:31:07.375
So dinner last night,
entertaining for the rest of us...

00:31:07.625 --> 00:31:09.917
...but for you, wow.
- What, last night?

00:31:10.125 --> 00:31:13.042
The whole dinner-theater/telenovela thing
you performed.

00:31:13.250 --> 00:31:16.000
- Telenovela?
- Yeah, Spanish-language sudser.

00:31:16.167 --> 00:31:18.542
Telemundo, dude. Univision.

00:31:18.750 --> 00:31:20.708
Victor, with the sexy
handlebar moustache.

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:26.333
So you still have the mindset
that you're the friend guy, huh?

00:31:26.542 --> 00:31:29.208
Befriending any beautiful woman
who cares to dine with us?

00:31:29.375 --> 00:31:32.667
- I'm working on it.
- Right. Well, if I may...

00:31:32.875 --> 00:31:35.542
...speaking from
a recent personal experience...

00:31:36.125 --> 00:31:40.083
...the triangle's not a friendly shape,
okay? It's pointy. It's got sharp edges.

00:31:40.292 --> 00:31:42.292
- Triangles hurt people.
- There's no triangle.

00:31:42.500 --> 00:31:44.708
Marissa and I aren't together.
Theresa's here for work.

00:31:44.917 --> 00:31:47.375
Except Marissa still obviously
has feelings for you...

00:31:47.583 --> 00:31:50.083
...and Theresa obviously
has feelings for you.

00:31:50.292 --> 00:31:54.208
In fact, the only thing that's not obvious
is how Ryan Atwood feels.

00:31:55.750 --> 00:31:58.083
- I don't know. It's complicated.
- It is complicated.

00:31:58.292 --> 00:32:01.625
It's complicated by the fact that
there's an Eddie who still obviously...

00:32:01.833 --> 00:32:05.542
...has feelings for Theresa. That would
actually make this romantic triangle...

00:32:05.750 --> 00:32:09.125
...more of a romantic rhombus.
- So, what am I supposed to do?

00:32:09.333 --> 00:32:12.083
That I don't know.
But I would do something soon...

00:32:12.292 --> 00:32:14.375
...otherwise someone's gonna get hurt.

00:32:15.417 --> 00:32:18.333
Judging from Eddie's phone voice,
it's probably gonna be you.

00:32:19.250 --> 00:32:21.042
What the hell do you expect, Sandy?

00:32:21.625 --> 00:32:25.375
Construction's a dirty business.
Bids accepted below cost.

00:32:25.583 --> 00:32:28.167
Permits mysteriously approved
at the last second.

00:32:28.375 --> 00:32:31.542
Guys like Shaun
are the lifeblood of the industry.

00:32:32.208 --> 00:32:35.208
Well, that was a touching speech, Cal,
but still the answer's no.

00:32:35.583 --> 00:32:37.125
Good luck.

00:32:37.333 --> 00:32:41.708
You're opening a Pandora's box,
you know that? Shaun's old. He's tired.

00:32:41.958 --> 00:32:45.042
If the DA starts asking questions,
he's got lots of answers.

00:32:45.208 --> 00:32:48.542
If you build your empire on quicksand,
sooner or later it's gonna sink.

00:32:48.750 --> 00:32:51.583
What about Kirsten?
She's complicit in all this too.

00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:54.958
- She doesn't know anything about this.
- Because I didn't tell her.

00:32:55.167 --> 00:32:58.292
I was trying to protect her.
But she's number two at Newport Group.

00:32:58.500 --> 00:33:00.708
She signs Shaun's paychecks.

00:33:00.917 --> 00:33:03.750
So like it or not,
we're in this mess together.

00:33:13.917 --> 00:33:15.292
Hey.

00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:17.208
Hi.

00:33:19.125 --> 00:33:22.542
Look, I'm sorry, okay?

00:33:22.750 --> 00:33:26.875
It's not like Cohen and I planned to
get together. It sort of just happened.

00:33:27.042 --> 00:33:30.125
And if it makes you feel better,
I don't think it's gonna work out.

00:33:30.917 --> 00:33:33.375
Well, that makes me feel great.

00:33:37.583 --> 00:33:40.750
I just can't be like one of those
couples, you know...

00:33:40.958 --> 00:33:43.875
...who hold hands in the hallway
and make out in between classes.

00:33:44.083 --> 00:33:46.417
Let the whole world
know what's going on.

00:33:46.625 --> 00:33:49.042
It's none of their business, you know?

00:33:49.333 --> 00:33:51.042
You don't have to ignore him, Summer.

00:33:51.250 --> 00:33:52.875
I don't ignore him.

00:33:53.042 --> 00:33:55.375
Okay, maybe a little,
but only in public.

00:33:55.583 --> 00:33:57.917
You spent so much time
trying to get his attention.

00:33:58.125 --> 00:34:00.042
I mean, you dressed up
as Wonder Woman.

00:34:00.750 --> 00:34:03.417
Well, Wonder Woman
is supposed to have an invisible jet...

00:34:04.042 --> 00:34:06.708
...not an invisible boyfriend.

00:34:07.958 --> 00:34:11.458
I mean, either you're really evil
or there's something else going on.

00:34:14.458 --> 00:34:16.833
I just don't know why he likes me.

00:34:17.250 --> 00:34:20.625
I mean, he's way smarter. And we have,
like, less than nothing in common.

00:34:20.833 --> 00:34:24.167
And he's just gonna get bored with me,
because, pretty much, all boys do.

00:34:24.750 --> 00:34:26.208
If everybody knows we're dating...

00:34:26.417 --> 00:34:29.000
...they'll know when he breaks up
with me, which he will.

00:34:32.167 --> 00:34:35.375
I mean, dumped by Seth Cohen?

00:34:35.583 --> 00:34:38.000
It's real good for my reputation.

00:34:41.417 --> 00:34:43.667
- Hello?
- Luke.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:47.917
- Hey, Mrs...
- Do not say my name out loud.

00:34:48.125 --> 00:34:50.458
Come to the motel.
Park across the street and walk.

00:34:50.667 --> 00:34:53.250
I'll get the same room.
Knock twice so I know it's you.

00:34:53.542 --> 00:34:54.542
And, Luke...

00:34:55.292 --> 00:34:56.542
...this is a booty call.

00:35:02.333 --> 00:35:05.833
It turns out you're not the only one
who's a coward.

00:35:06.083 --> 00:35:09.208
- Oh, it's nice to see you also, yeah?
- Summer's scared too.

00:35:09.417 --> 00:35:11.667
I know. She's scared to be seen
in public with me.

00:35:11.875 --> 00:35:14.625
Come on, Cohen. She fought for you.
She was fearless.

00:35:14.875 --> 00:35:18.167
Ruthless, in fact.
Now she's got you.

00:35:18.417 --> 00:35:20.208
There's nothing scarier than that.

00:35:20.667 --> 00:35:23.958
Nothing scarier than being with me,
or do you mean, like, anyone?

00:35:24.167 --> 00:35:26.542
Look, once you get what you want...

00:35:26.750 --> 00:35:28.708
...that's when you've got
something to lose.

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:30.917
She's afraid of losing you, Cohen.

00:35:31.125 --> 00:35:32.833
Why? I'm not going anywhere.

00:35:33.167 --> 00:35:34.833
Maybe you need to let her know that.

00:36:00.375 --> 00:36:02.542
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:36:02.750 --> 00:36:05.417
Can we talk?
I know it's weird, me being here...

00:36:05.583 --> 00:36:09.542
...but I just really needed to know...
- Am I still in love with Ryan?

00:36:11.500 --> 00:36:13.125
Because you still are.

00:36:13.583 --> 00:36:15.292
I don't wanna be.

00:36:15.500 --> 00:36:18.583
It would be a whole lot easier
if I wasn't.

00:36:46.250 --> 00:36:48.458
- Hey, man. What's up?
- Hey.

00:36:50.667 --> 00:36:52.875
It's a long drive just to come say hello.

00:36:53.667 --> 00:36:56.083
Last night, when you asked me
about Theresa...

00:36:56.292 --> 00:36:58.458
...I wasn't completely honest.

00:37:01.125 --> 00:37:02.750
Carl.

00:37:03.375 --> 00:37:06.208
- I'm gonna take a break, all right?
- Okay.

00:37:16.542 --> 00:37:19.833
- So why lie?
- I'm sorry, man. I didn't...

00:37:20.625 --> 00:37:23.875
- She staying with you?
- No. She's working, like her mom said.

00:37:26.125 --> 00:37:28.083
Still, I...

00:37:28.292 --> 00:37:30.708
I mean, I pop the question...

00:37:30.917 --> 00:37:32.833
...and she runs away...

00:37:34.042 --> 00:37:35.875
...to you.

00:37:36.708 --> 00:37:38.542
Married?

00:37:39.250 --> 00:37:42.708
- Wow.
- Yeah, that's the plan.

00:37:43.417 --> 00:37:45.792
You must really love him a lot.

00:37:47.167 --> 00:37:48.375
Do you love her?

00:37:50.375 --> 00:37:52.875
- I don't know.
- Yeah, well, I do.

00:37:53.083 --> 00:37:54.792
Okay? I do.

00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:57.667
And I wanna take care of her.
Do you?

00:37:57.875 --> 00:37:59.583
I mean, can you?

00:38:00.583 --> 00:38:03.333
Look, I know this is tough. L...

00:38:04.833 --> 00:38:07.333
I can't tell you what to do.

00:38:08.292 --> 00:38:10.750
But if you wanted to,
you could talk to her.

00:38:10.958 --> 00:38:12.958
You know, convince her to come home.

00:38:13.167 --> 00:38:17.208
Otherwise, be ready to fight for her,
because I'm not just gonna walk away.

00:38:17.375 --> 00:38:19.083
I can't.

00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:24.833
You got a long ride home.

00:38:26.167 --> 00:38:27.542
You got a lot to think about.

00:38:32.208 --> 00:38:35.208
In the church where my mom goes,
there's a stained glass window...

00:38:35.417 --> 00:38:37.208
...of Teresa of Avila.

00:38:38.042 --> 00:38:40.375
Her heart's being pierced
by the arrow of an angel.

00:38:41.542 --> 00:38:42.917
Her eyes are closed.

00:38:43.417 --> 00:38:46.083
And even though it hurts her
to love that much...

00:38:46.292 --> 00:38:48.083
...she has the most beautiful smile.

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:52.917
I remember my first communion.

00:38:53.125 --> 00:38:55.333
I was wearing a white dress and gloves.

00:38:55.542 --> 00:38:58.208
And I looked up at that window
and I thought...

00:38:58.375 --> 00:39:01.208
... someday someone
would pierce my heart...

00:39:02.333 --> 00:39:05.458
...and I would walk down the aisle
in a real white dress...

00:39:05.667 --> 00:39:07.542
...and understand why she's smiling.

00:39:14.417 --> 00:39:15.875
I know it sounds lame.

00:39:19.792 --> 00:39:22.542
But I guess life's not really like that.

00:39:23.792 --> 00:39:27.167
You can't get caught up in wishing
for something that's not gonna happen.

00:39:27.750 --> 00:39:30.583
You gotta hold on to the next best thing.

00:39:37.083 --> 00:39:39.375
I guess I should call Eddie.

00:39:39.917 --> 00:39:42.833
Yeah.
I should get back to school.

00:39:51.458 --> 00:39:52.708
So thanks.

00:39:53.083 --> 00:39:55.750
I can see why Ryan likes it here.

00:40:09.583 --> 00:40:12.583
Here you go. Full refund.
Thanks for coming. The show's over.

00:40:12.750 --> 00:40:14.875
Thanks so much, though.
It was great having you.

00:40:15.083 --> 00:40:17.625
- This kid bothering you, Summer?
- No, it's okay. Thanks.

00:40:17.833 --> 00:40:19.375
- Thanks.
- You're making a scene.

00:40:19.583 --> 00:40:21.500
- I need to talk to you.
- I'll IM you later.

00:40:22.625 --> 00:40:24.333
Okay.

00:40:28.875 --> 00:40:30.500
- Let's talk up here.
- Oh, my God. No.

00:40:30.958 --> 00:40:33.042
- Summer, I know you're scared.
- Yeah, of you.

00:40:33.250 --> 00:40:36.542
You kiss these other guys, but you won't
kiss me? Acknowledge me now...

00:40:36.750 --> 00:40:39.000
...or lose me forever.
- You're dating this emo geek?

00:40:39.208 --> 00:40:41.542
Yes, Brad, she's dating this emo geek.

00:40:41.750 --> 00:40:45.875
Yeah, that's right. I'm a big dork
and I listen to emo. And I'm dating her.

00:40:46.083 --> 00:40:50.042
- Why are you doing this?
- Because, Summer, I like you this much.

00:40:50.292 --> 00:40:53.125
And if you don't feel
the same way about me, then...

00:40:53.625 --> 00:40:56.458
Someone will have to give me
a hand down. It's high up here...

00:40:56.625 --> 00:40:59.875
...and I could fall and that would be
embarrassing. More embarrassing.

00:41:19.667 --> 00:41:21.458
I can't believe this.

00:41:21.625 --> 00:41:25.083
It's all over but the big,
public make-out session.

00:41:38.167 --> 00:41:39.708
That'll be 10 bucks, Cohen.

00:41:39.917 --> 00:41:42.208
That's for a worthy cause.

00:41:44.542 --> 00:41:46.875
Hey, Carl, can I talk to Eddie?

00:41:47.083 --> 00:41:50.083
Yeah. Yeah, I'll hold on.

00:41:58.958 --> 00:42:00.792
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:02.208
You packing?

00:42:03.667 --> 00:42:05.208
Yeah.

00:42:05.917 --> 00:42:08.292
I think I should probably go home.

00:42:08.500 --> 00:42:11.167
Seems like the right thing to do, right?

00:42:11.833 --> 00:42:15.625
You gotta do what's right for you.
You and Eddie.

00:42:15.833 --> 00:42:18.500
I gotta figure out what's right for me...

00:42:18.667 --> 00:42:20.042
...and Marissa.

00:42:20.792 --> 00:42:22.417
Right.

00:42:25.417 --> 00:42:28.167
So if it's the right thing to do,
why don't I want you to go?

00:42:30.417 --> 00:42:32.542
Why don't I wanna go?

00:42:40.167 --> 00:42:42.333
I can think of a reason.

00:42:54.250 --> 00:42:55.875
Hello?

00:42:56.250 --> 00:42:57.875
Hello?

00:42:58.250 --> 00:43:00.042
Theresa, are you there?

00:43:00.458 --> 00:43:02.250
Theresa?
